# Experimental single-circle fitter. Total XY budget = 2*$12; no cap allowance.

= three point circles S @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J3 P3 Q3
pos -90 -100 -10

= three point circles loop @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-5 Y0 I-20 J30 P20 Q30
pos -105 -100 -10

= collinear reversal must not skip hidden travel @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y0 I-30 J0 P40 Q0
pos -110 -100 -10

= coincident start handle @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I0 J0 P2 Q4
pos -90 -100 -10

= near straight large radius takes line fallback @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I3 J0.000001 P3 Q0.000001
pos -90 -100 -10

= tiny curve @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X0.01 Y0 I0.003 J0.01 P0.003 Q0.01
pos -99.99 -100 -10

= hidden inflection with large endpoint @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X-10 Y8550 I-3.3333 J16.6667 P3.3333 Q-9016.667
pos -110 8450 -10

= cap rejection queues nothing @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5 X10 Y0 I100000 J100000 P100000 Q100000 -> error:38
pos -100 -100 -10

= supported G5.1 conversion @circle
G10 L20 P1 X0 Y0 Z0
F1000
G5.1 X10 Y0 I3 J4
pos -90 -100 -10
